From e82b35ccb4888f84f99533d31280af245ac7e1a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:43:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] Lab: XCL_SPARSE_MAP_NOWAIT=1 - a Map's copy back on a
 copy queue of its own

A title's Map of sparse memory (readback_now) copies the range back on
the sparse queue and waits for it. That DIRECT queue shares the 3D
engine with the title's lists, so each Map waited for them (PROF1: 226
ms a frame of waits in readback_released, behind one READBACK lock).

With the switch, the copy goes on an unadopted COPY queue (made with
the device's original creators, so the title's ExecuteCommandLists
hook and list_x's queues never see it) that first waits on the GPU for
a signal of the sparse queue after everything submitted to it so far:
the Map's CPU writes uploaded, tiles mapped and cleared. It reads what
the copy on the sparse queue reads; later sparse queue work is not
ordered after it, as a copy back is a snapshot taken after the Map was
called. If the queue cannot be made or ordered, the old path runs.
A Map of a range none of whose tiles has video memory returns after
the earlier copies back are landed: the copy would copy nothing.

Not done: skipping the copy when the asynchronous copies back cover
the range. Those cover only what the title's copies, fills and value
writes wrote (list_x note_write), not its shaders' writes, which only
the Map's copy brings back: the skip could return stale bytes.

Tests: the same parts and bytes on both queues; the Map copy does not
run before gated work on the sparse queue; the switch is off unless 1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
